{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nAfter the outbound child, a release name the Jira project lacks (never created, deleted, renamed, or archived) is sent as a per-item add, Jira rejects it with HTTP 400, and `_update_one_dispatch_releases` only logs that to stderr every pass. Nobody looking at the ticket can see why the release is not in Jira. The operator decided on 2026-11-05 (epic comment) that the bridge must not write such a name, must keep it on the rebar ticket, must raise a `BRIDGE_ALERT` naming the missing version, must retry each pass, and must never create Jira versions. ADR 0124 decisions 8 and 9 add the archived-version rule and the alert lifecycle.\n\n## Approach\n\n1. **Read the project's versions.** Add `get_project_versions(project_key) -> list[dict]` (each `{\"name\": str, \"archived\": bool}`) to the `TicketTransport` protocol in `src/rebar/reconciler/_backend.py`:\n   - Cloud, in `src/rebar/reconciler/adapters/jira/acli_rest.py`: `self._direct_rest_get(f\"/rest/api/3/project/{key}/versions\")`, which Atlassian documents as returning all versions unpaginated.\n   - Data Center, in `src/rebar/reconciler/adapters/jira_datacenter/_issues.py`: `self._client.project_versions(key)` (pycontribs `JIRA.project_versions(project) -> list[Version]`), mapped through `_unwrap`.\n   Read once per bound project per pass in `src/rebar/reconciler/outbound_pass.py`, beside the intent computation (lines 83-93), and pass a `release_availability: dict[str, dict[str, str]] | None` (project → name → `\"available\"|\"archived\"`) on `OutboundDiffConfig`. A transport failure for a project leaves that project's entry absent, which means \"unknown\": nothing is withheld or alerted for it that pass, so a Jira outage cannot fire alerts.\n2. **Withhold in the diff.** `_diff_releases` (`src/rebar/reconciler/outbound_releases.py`, from the outbound child) takes the ticket's project availability map. For an ADD whose name is absent from the map (missing) or archived, it emits no Jira add and instead returns a withheld record `{\"release\": name, \"reason\": \"missing\"|\"archived\"}`. REMOVEs are unaffected. Withheld names are still recorded as outbound adds in `inbound_differ._build_outbound_context`, so the same-pass inbound REMOVE is suppressed and the name stays on the rebar ticket.\n3. **Alert lifecycle.** New module `src/rebar/reconciler/release_alerts.py`:\n   - `plan_release_alerts(ticket, withheld, availability_known) -> list[dict]` is pure. It compares the withheld names with the ticket's unresolved `bridge_alerts` whose reason starts with `release-version-`. It returns a new alert `{\"reason\": \"release-version-<missing|archived>:<name>\", \"tag\": \"release-version-<missing|archived>\", \"release\": name}` for each withheld name without an unresolved alert of the same reason, and a resolution `{\"resolved\": true, \"resolves_uuid\": <uuid>, \"reason\": <same reason>}` for each unresolved release alert whose name is no longer withheld (written to Jira, removed from the ticket, or now available). When availability is unknown it returns `[]`.\n   - The pass runs it for every bound ticket whose project availability is known and that has local releases or an unresolved release alert, and writes each record as a `BRIDGE_ALERT` event through the reconciler's existing event writer (`inbound_translate._write_event_file`, line 136). The reducer already folds both shapes (`src/rebar/reducer/_processors.py:241-273`). Steady state writes nothing.\n   Hook the call into `run_differs.py` after outbound mutations are computed (`_run_differs_inbound`, line 305 onward, where `outbound_raw` is available), in a helper so `run_differs` stays within its complexity ceiling.\n4. **Never create versions.** No code path calls a version-create endpoint; a test asserts the fake transports never receive one.\n5. **Docs.** In `docs/jira-sync-setup.md`, add a short \"Fix versions\" subsection: versions must exist in the Jira project (created by people, never by the bridge), the alert names, the retry, the archived rule, and the prerequisites (Fix versions editable for the bridge account; see ADR 0124 Evidence about screen checks).\n\n## Scope\n\n- `src/rebar/reconciler/_backend.py`\n- `src/rebar/reconciler/adapters/jira/acli_rest.py`\n- `src/rebar/reconciler/adapters/jira_datacenter/_issues.py`\n- `src/rebar/reconciler/outbound_pass.py`\n- `src/rebar/reconciler/outbound_differ.py` (`OutboundDiffConfig` field)\n- `src/rebar/reconciler/outbound_releases.py`\n- `src/rebar/reconciler/inbound_differ.py`\n- `src/rebar/reconciler/release_alerts.py` (new)\n- `src/rebar/reconciler/run_differs.py`\n- `docs/jira-sync-setup.md`\n- `tests/unit/reconciler/test_release_alerts.py` (new)\n- `tests/unit/reconciler/diffing/test_outbound_releases.py` (extend)\n- `tests/unit/reconciler/mutate/test_fix_version_transport.py` (extend: version-list reads)\n- `tests/integration/reconciler/test_reconcile_releases_roundtrip.py` (extend)\n\n## Testing\n\n- `plan_release_alerts`: withheld `2.4` with no alert yields one new alert with reason `release-version-missing:2.4`; the same input with that alert unresolved yields `[]`; an unresolved alert for `2.4` with `2.4` no longer withheld yields one resolution carrying its uuid; an archived name yields reason `release-version-archived:2.4`; unknown availability yields `[]`.\n- Diff: a missing name produces no Jira add and one withheld record; an archived name likewise; an available name is added; a REMOVE of an archived name is still emitted.\n- Suppression: a withheld name is not removed locally by the same-pass inbound diff.\n- Transports: Cloud reads `GET /rest/api/3/project/REB/versions`; DC calls `project_versions(\"REB\")`; a transport error yields unknown availability.\n- Integration, multi-pass: pass 1 with a local release `2.4` and a project without it writes one alert and no Jira add; pass 2 unchanged writes nothing; the version then appears in the project; pass 3 writes the Jira add and one resolving alert; pass 4 writes nothing. No fake transport ever receives a version-create call.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] A rebar release naming a version the Jira project lacks is not written to Jira, stays on the rebar ticket, and gets exactly one unresolved `BRIDGE_ALERT` whose reason names it; pinned by the multi-pass integration test.\n- [ ] Each later pass retries, and once the version exists the name is written and the alert is resolved in that same pass; pinned by the same test.\n- [ ] An archived version is withheld with reason `release-version-archived:<name>`; pinned by tests.\n- [ ] A failed version-list read writes no alert and resolves none; pinned by a test.\n- [ ] No bridge code path creates a Jira version; pinned by the fake-transport assertion.\n- [ ] `docs/jira-sync-setup.md` documents the alert, the retry and the version prerequisite.\n- [ ] `python scripts/check_complexity_baseline.py --check` and `python scripts/check_mechanism_delta.py --check` exit 0, and no `src/rebar` file exceeds 800 lines.\n- [ ] `env -u JIRA_URL -u JIRA_USER -u JIRA_API_TOKEN make verify` exits 0 on the commit pushed for review."}},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1794264686631451001,"uuid":"1703aaf2-6b87-49d6-b6e9-faf8809f96a5"}